    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<p>Red kidney beans are a well-known food material, commonly included in popular dishes like eight-treasure congee. So, what exactly are red kidney beans? Let me provide a detailed introduction.</p><figure id="attachment_496-2" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-496-2" style="width: 735px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img src="/images/Red-Kidney-Beans-300x223.jpg" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-496" alt="Red Kidney Beans" width="745" height="554" title="What are Red Kidney Beans? Do You Really Know? 6" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-496-2" class="wp-caption-text">Red Kidney Beans</figcaption></figure><div id="ez-toc-container" class="ez-toc-v2_0_85 counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-grey ez-toc-container-direction"><div class="ez-toc-title-container"><p class="ez-toc-title" style="cursor:inherit">Table of Contents</p>
<span class="ez-toc-title-toggle"><a href="#" class="ez-toc-pull-right ez-toc-btn ez-toc-btn-xs ez-toc-btn-default ez-toc-toggle" aria-label="Toggle Table of Content"><span class="ez-toc-js-icon-con"><span class=""><span class="eztoc-hide" style="display:none;">Toggle</span><span class="ez-toc-icon-toggle-span"><svg style="fill: #999;color:#999" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="list-377408" width="20px" height="20px" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M6 6H4v2h2V6zm14 0H8v2h12V6zM4 11h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2zM4 16h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><svg style="fill: #999;color:#999" class="arrow-unsorted-368013" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10px" height="10px" viewBox="0 0 24 24" version="1.2" baseProfile="tiny"><path d="M18.2 9.3l-6.2-6.3-6.2 6.3c-.2.2-.3.4-.3.7s.1.5.3.7c.2.2.4.3.7.3h11c.3 0 .5-.1.7-.3.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7zM5.8 14.7l6.2 6.3 6.2-6.3c.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7c-.2-.2-.4-.3-.7-.3h-11c-.3 0-.5.1-.7.3-.2.2-.3.5-.3.7s.1.5.3.7z"/></svg></span></span></span></a></span></div><nav><ul class='ez-toc-list ez-toc-list-level-1 ' ><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-1" href="#What_are_Red_Kidney_Beans_Origin_and_Distribution" >What are Red Kidney Beans? Origin and Distribution.</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-2" href="#Nutritional_Structure_of_Red_Kidney_Beans" >Nutritional Structure of Red Kidney Beans</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-3" href="#Are_Red_Kidney_Beans_and_Dark_Red_Kidney_Beans_the_Same_Variety" >Are Red Kidney Beans and Dark Red Kidney Beans the Same Variety?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-4" href="#What_is_the_International_Production_Volume_of_Red_Kidney_Beans" >What is the International Production Volume of Red Kidney Beans?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-5" href="#Distribution_of_Red_Kidney_Bean_Production_in_China" >Distribution of Red Kidney Bean Production in China</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-6" href="#How_to_Find_High-Quality_Red_Kidney_Bean_Suppliers" >How to Find High-Quality Red Kidney Bean Suppliers?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-7" href="#What_are_the_Advantages_of_Hebei_in_Bulk_Trade_Export_of_Red_Kidney_Beans" >What are the Advantages of Hebei in Bulk Trade Export of Red Kidney Beans?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-8" href="#What_is_the_Price_Advantage_of_Bulk_Trade_of_Hebei_Red_Kidney_Beans" >What is the Price Advantage of Bulk Trade of Hebei Red Kidney Beans?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-9" href="#How_to_Choose_Quality_Red_Kidney_Beans" >How to Choose Quality Red Kidney Beans?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-10" href="#How_to_Store_Red_Kidney_Beans_What_is_their_Shelf_Life" >How to Store Red Kidney Beans? What is their Shelf Life?</a></li></ul></nav></div><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_are_Red_Kidney_Beans_Origin_and_Distribution"></span>What are Red Kidney Beans? Origin and Distribution.<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>Red kidney beans are a type of legume named for their shape and color, which resemble a kidney. They are rich in protein, fats, carbohydrates, calcium, and various B vitamins, making them highly nutritious food.</p><p>The main production areas of red kidney beans are concentrated in several provinces in China. Shanxi Province is one of the primary producers, particularly in Kelan County and Wuzhai County. Due to its unique geographical location and climate conditions. The red kidney beans produced here are large, bright, sweet in taste, warm in nature, high in calcium, low in sugar, and high in fiber while low in fat, making them a recognized green and pollution-free food.</p><p>Additionally, Hebei Province, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, and Heilongjiang Province are also important areas for red kidney bean cultivation. The Zhangjiakou area in Hebei Province, including Huai&#8217;an, Yangyuan, and Zhuolu, has significant red kidney bean production. There is also some cultivation in Inner Mongolia and Heilongjiang.</p><p>Overall, the main production areas for red kidney beans in China include Kelan and Wuzhai Counties in Shanxi, Zhangjiakou in Hebei, Inner Mongolia, and Heilongjiang. The climate and soil conditions in these regions are very suitable for growing red kidney beans, making them the primary cultivation areas.</p><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Nutritional_Structure_of_Red_Kidney_Beans"></span>Nutritional Structure of Red Kidney Beans<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>Red kidney beans are favored for their undeniable nutritional value. They are a nutrient-dense food, which can be analyzed in terms of protein, carbohydrates, fiber, fats, vitamins, and minerals.</p><ul><li><strong>Protein:</strong> Red kidney beans have a high protein content, with approximately 23.1 grams of protein per 100 grams, as noted in a 2011 report on Sina News. The quality of this protein is high and similar to animal protein, making it an important nutritional source for the human body. They contain a complete range of amino acids, including all eight essential amino acids.</li><li><strong>Carbohydrates:</strong> Red kidney beans also have a high carbohydrate content, with about 56.9 grams per 100 grams. Most of these are complex carbohydrates, including starch and small amounts of natural sugars. These carbohydrates provide energy for the body and help maintain stable blood sugar levels.</li><li><strong>Fiber:</strong> They are rich in dietary fiber, with around 8.3 grams of crude fiber per 100 grams. Dietary fiber helps promote intestinal peristalsis, improve constipation, and maintain gut health.</li><li><strong>Fats:</strong> Red kidney beans are low in fat, containing only about 1.3 grams per 100 grams. The fats present are primarily beneficial monounsaturated and polyunsaturated fatty acids, which have various health benefits, such as lowering cholesterol and reducing the risk of cardiovascular diseases.</li><li><strong>Vitamins:</strong> They are rich in vitamins, including B vitamins (such as B1, B2), vitamin C, and vitamin E. These vitamins play important roles in immune function, skin health, and antioxidant activity.</li><li><strong>Minerals:</strong> Red kidney beans are abundant in various minerals like calcium, iron, potassium, and magnesium. Their calcium content is particularly high, exceeding that of chicken by more than seven times, while their iron content is four times that of chicken. These minerals contribute to bone health, blood production, and electrolyte balance.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Are_Red_Kidney_Beans_and_Dark_Red_Kidney_Beans_the_Same_Variety"></span>Are Red Kidney Beans and Dark Red Kidney Beans the Same Variety?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><figure id="attachment_497-2" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-497-2" style="width: 614px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img src="/images/dark-red-kidney-beans-300x295.jpg" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-497" alt="dark red kidney beans" width="624" height="614" title="What are Red Kidney Beans? Do You Really Know? 7" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-497-2" class="wp-caption-text">dark red kidney beans</figcaption></figure><p>Red kidney beans and dark red kidney beans are not entirely the same but do overlap. Dark red kidney beans (also known as British red) are a type of red kidney bean, as confirmed by multiple sources. For instance, the China Small Grains Network mentions that &#8221; the types of red kidney beans include dark red kidney beans, small red kidney beans, and purple flower kidney beans,&#8221; and the Agricultural Data Center details the characteristics and origins of dark red kidney beans. This indicates that dark red kidney beans are a subclass of red kidney beans, while red kidney beans encompass a broader classification, including various types, including dark red kidney beans.</p><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_is_the_International_Production_Volume_of_Red_Kidney_Beans"></span>What is the International Production Volume of Red Kidney Beans?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>Here are some production figures for red kidney beans from various countries:</p><ul><li><strong>India:</strong> India is the largest producer and consumer of red kidney beans in the world.</li><li><strong>Australia:</strong> The production is nearly 250,000 tons, mostly from South Australia and Victoria.</li><li><strong>Ethiopia:</strong> In the 2016/2017 main planting season, the average yield was 1.69 tons per hectare.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Distribution_of_Red_Kidney_Bean_Production_in_China"></span>Distribution of Red Kidney Bean Production in China<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>The production and distribution of red kidney beans in China are as follows:</p><ul><li><strong>Production:</strong> In recent years, Sichuan Province&#8217;s red kidney bean production has exceeded 10,000 tons, mainly distributed in Hanyuan, Shimian, Baoxing, Lushan, Liangshan Prefecture, and Guangyuan. Shanxi Province serves as the national export base for red kidney beans, with an area of about 230,000 acres dedicated to cultivation, and an annual export volume of 30,000 tons, accounting for over 50% of the national export volume of kidney beans. Heilongjiang Province has the largest variety and quantity of kidney beans produced in China, with an annual production of 300,000 tons.</li><li><strong>Distribution:</strong> Red kidney beans are widely cultivated across China, primarily in Northeast, and North China, Shaanxi, Hubei, Anhui, Jiangsu, Sichuan, and Yunnan. Specific regions include Wuzhai County in Xinzhou, Shanxi (Wuzhai red kidney beans), which has rich water systems and ample sunlight, making it suitable for red kidney bean cultivation. The northern part of Shanxi, central Hebei, and Inner Mongolia are also major planting areas. In Sichuan Province, red kidney beans are mainly found in Hanyuan, Shimian, Baoxing, Lushan, Liangshan Prefecture, and Guangyuan. The western and southeastern parts of Heilongjiang Province are also important growing areas for red kidney beans.</li></ul><p>China&#8217;s red kidney bean production is high, concentrated mainly in Sichuan, Shanxi, and Heilongjiang, with a wide distribution and a long cultivation history.</p><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="How_to_Find_High-Quality_Red_Kidney_Bean_Suppliers"></span>How to Find High-Quality Red Kidney Bean Suppliers?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>To find high-quality red kidney bean suppliers, you can focus on two aspects: origin and certification.</p><ul><li><strong>Choice of Origin</strong><br />
Kelan County and Wuzhai County in Shanxi Province are among the main production areas for red kidney beans. The beans from these regions are known for their unique geographical and climatic conditions, resulting in large, brightly colored, and nutrient-rich beans that have passed the national pollution-free agricultural product certification. Furthermore, the red kidney beans from Wuzhai County in Xinzhou have received the national geographical indication certification, indicating that their quality is officially recognized.</li><li><strong>Certification</strong><br />
Choosing suppliers with good certifications is crucial. For example, Dacang Food Company has over thirty years of experience in processing and exporting kidney beans and is a stable supplier of high quality to global customers. Additionally, the red kidney beans from Loufan County have been certified as organic agricultural products by the international ecological organization &#8220;ECOCERT,&#8221; receiving this certification for several consecutive years, which ensures the quality and safety of their products.</li><li><strong>Online Platforms and Bidding Information</strong><br />
You can also find quality suppliers through specialized online platforms and bidding announcements. For instance, the Food Business Network lists several manufacturers and suppliers of red kidney beans, allowing you to filter by origin, company establishment date, and company size. You can also pay attention to bidding announcements, such as the selective bidding announcement for red kidney bean processing enterprises from Wahaha, which typically lists qualified high-quality suppliers.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_are_the_Advantages_of_Hebei_in_Bulk_Trade_Export_of_Red_Kidney_Beans"></span>What are the Advantages of Hebei in Bulk Trade Export of Red Kidney Beans?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><figure id="attachment_498-2" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-498-2" style="width: 730px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img src="/images/red-kidney-peas-300x187.jpg" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-498" alt="Red kidney bean harvest in Kelan County, Shanxi Province" width="740" height="461" title="What are Red Kidney Beans? Do You Really Know? 8" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-498-2" class="wp-caption-text">Red kidney bean harvest in Kelan County, Shanxi Province</figcaption></figure><p>Hebei Province has significant advantages in the bulk trade export of red kidney beans, mainly reflected in quality, yield, and transportation.</p><ul><li><strong>Quality:</strong> The red kidney beans produced in Hebei are of high quality. Kangbao County has introduced superior varieties and implements standardized planting, resulting in pure-colored, high-quality beans. It has become the largest red kidney bean production base in Zhangjiakou and exports to countries and regions such as Pakistan and Southeast Asia. Additionally, Hebei Nihewan Agricultural Development Co., Ltd. has developed a quality inspection system for red kidney bean production and processing to ensure their quality and safety.</li><li><strong>Yield:</strong> Hebei Province ranks among the top in the country in terms of both the planting area and yield of red kidney beans. In the northern regions of Hebei, such as Huai&#8217;an, Yangyuan, Zhuolu, and Yuxian in Zhangjiakou, about 2,000 tons of yellow kidney beans are produced, while the Bashang region (Zhangbei, Kangbao, and Guyuan) produces over 10,000 tons of small red kidney beans. The annual export volume of red kidney beans from Hebei Province is about 30,000 tons, accounting for over 30% of the national export volume, demonstrating Hebei&#8217;s strong production capacity.</li><li><strong>Transportation and Trade:</strong> The geographical location and transportation conditions of Hebei Province also facilitate the export of red kidney beans. Located in northern China, it is close to major transportation hubs like Tianjin Port or Qingdao Port, making it easy to ship red kidney beans to international markets. The red kidney beans from Kangbao County have gradually become a prosperous industry that connects households domestically and accesses international markets. Additionally, farmers in Hebei have improved their earnings by expanding the cultivation of red kidney beans and enhancing their responsiveness to international market demands.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_is_the_Price_Advantage_of_Bulk_Trade_of_Hebei_Red_Kidney_Beans"></span>What is the Price Advantage of Bulk Trade of Hebei Red Kidney Beans?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>The price advantage of Hebei&#8217;s bulk trade in red kidney beans is reflected in several aspects:</p><ul><li><strong>Advantage of Main Production Area:</strong> As a major production area for red kidney beans, Hebei has geographical and climatic advantages that allow for large-scale cultivation, ensuring both yield and quality. This geographical advantage provides Hebei red kidney beans with a certain degree of price competitiveness in the market.</li><li><strong>Complete Industry Chain:</strong> The cultivation, procurement, processing, and sales of Hebei red kidney beans form a complete industry chain. From farmers directly selling beans to trade companies and then to bulk trade, each link is effectively managed and optimized, reducing costs in the intermediate stages and improving overall price competitiveness.</li><li><strong>Combination of Market and Reserve:</strong> The bulk trade of Hebei red kidney beans combines market and reserve strategies. Through scientific reserve management, it ensures stable supply and price stability of red kidney beans during different seasons and market fluctuations. This reserve mechanism not only guarantees market supply but also enhances the price competitiveness of red kidney beans.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="How_to_Choose_Quality_Red_Kidney_Beans"></span><strong>How to Choose Quality Red Kidney Beans?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><figure id="attachment_499-2" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-499-2" style="width: 671px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img src="/images/red-kidney-peas-2-300x199.jpg" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-499" alt="Red kidney peas " width="681" height="452" title="What are Red Kidney Beans? Do You Really Know? 9" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-499-2" class="wp-caption-text">Red kidney peas</figcaption></figure><p>When selecting quality red kidney beans, consider the following aspects:</p><ul><li><strong>Color:</strong> Quality red kidney beans should have the inherent bright color of the variety. If the beans are vibrant and glossy, it indicates good quality; dull or lackluster beans may be of inferior quality.</li><li><strong>Texture:</strong> Full and uniformly shaped beans are important characteristics of high-quality red kidney beans. Beans that are shriveled, incomplete, uneven in size, or have broken or missing parts are of lower quality. Additionally, good red kidney beans should be dry and clear, with no signs of pests or mold.</li><li><strong>Shape:</strong> Red kidney beans come in various shapes, including kidney-shaped, oval, flat, cylindrical, and round. Beans that are bright and uniform in color are generally of better quality.</li><li><strong>Storage Condition:</strong> Quality red kidney beans should be dry and free of threads, indicating good storage conditions. By assessing these factors, you can accurately select high-quality red kidney beans.</li></ul><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="How_to_Store_Red_Kidney_Beans_What_is_their_Shelf_Life"></span>How to Store Red Kidney Beans? What is their Shelf Life?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p>The storage methods and shelf life of red kidney beans are as follows:</p><p><strong>1. Storage Methods:</strong></p><p>Store in a Cool, Dry Place: Red kidney beans should be kept in a cool, dry location away from moisture and direct sunlight to prevent mold and spoilage.<br />
<strong>Refrigeration:</strong> Steam the beans until semi-cooked, cool them, seal them in a fresh-keeping bag, and store them in the refrigerator to extend their shelf life.<br />
<strong>Freezing:</strong> Seal the beans in a fresh-keeping bag and store them in the freezer; this can keep them good for a year.</p><p><strong>2. Shelf Life:</strong> The typical shelf life of red kidney beans is 12 months to 1 year. However, if stored properly, they can last 1 to 3 years. The specific shelf life may vary based on brand and packaging, with some brands having a shelf life of 365 days while others may last 18 months.</p><p>That concludes the summary of knowledge about red kidney beans.</p>`} />
